  "version": "2026-09-07.1",
  "note": "One entry per thread per run. `match` is the Message-ID of any message in the thread; the run resolves it to that thread's key. `request_type` uses two labels the model never produces -- `ignored` and `quarantined` -- so that a message the gate stopped is scored in the same confusion matrix as one the model classified. A phishing mail that reached the model is then a recall miss on `quarantined`, which is the number the phishing gate reads. `priority` is 0 for anything the gate stopped, because priority is only computed for classified threads.",
